      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Irish immigrants from County Clare began arriving in Maple Lake in the late 1850s and early 1860s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://ci.maple-lake.mn.us/about",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first lots were sold to John Roehrenbach, who opened a dry goods and groceries store on Easy Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ci.maple-lake.mn.us/about",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Soo Line railroad expanded through Maple Lake, and an elevator opened in 1889, spurring growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ci.maple-lake.mn.us/about",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 1910s, Maple Lake built a water tower, water mains, and sewers, and welcomed its first car.",
